itics, he was a banker and businessman.","image":"Gaston Browne Coronation 2023.jpg","birth":1967.1068493150685,"death":null},"Q9682":{"label":"Elizabeth II","description":"Queen of the United Kingdom from 1952 to 2022 (1926–2022)","enwiki":"Elizabeth II","summary":"Elizabeth II (Elizabeth Alexandra Mary; 21 April 1926 – 8 September 2022) was Queen of the United Kingdom and other Commonwealth realms from 6 February 1952 until her death in 2022. She was queen regnant of 32 sovereign states during her lifetime and was the monarch of 15 realms at her death. Her reign of 70 years and 214 days is the longest of any British monarch, the second-longest of any sovereign state, and the longest of any queen regnant in history.\nElizabeth was born in Mayfair, London, during the reign of her paternal grandfather, King George V. She was the first child of the Duke and Duchess of York (later King George VI and Queen Elizabeth the Queen Mother).","image":"Queen Elizabeth II official portrait for 1959 tour (retouched) (cropped) (3-to-4 aspect ratio).jpg","birth":1926.3013698630136,"death":2022.6849315068494},"Q17566330":{"label":"Rodney Williams","description":"Governor-General of Antigua and Barbuda (born 1947)","enwiki":"Rodney Williams","summary":"Sir Rodney Errey Lawrence Williams,  (born 2 November 1947) is an Antiguan politician who is the fourth and current governor-general of Antigua and Barbuda, having previously served as Minister for Education, Culture and Technology and as a Member of Parliament until 2004.","image":"Governor General Of Antigua And Barbuda (37250652361) (cropped).jpg","birth":1947.835616438356,"death":null},"Q232610":{"label":"Louise Lake-Tack","description":"Governor-General of Antigua and Barbuda","enwiki":"Louise Lake-Tack","summary":"Dame Louise Agnetha Lake-Tack (born 26 July 1944) who served as the third governor-general of Antigua and Barbuda from 2007 to 2014. She was the first woman to hold the office.","image":"DameLouiseLake-Tack.jpg","birth":1944.5655737704917,"death":null},"Q431167":{"label":"James Carlisle","description":"Dentist, former Governor-General of Antigua and Barbuda","enwiki":"James Carlisle","summary":"Sir James Beethoven Carlisle, GCMG (born 5 August 1937) is an Antiguan politician and dentist who served as the second governor-general of Antigua and Barbuda from 1993 to 2007. Selected by Vere Cornwall Bird (the country's first prime minister), his term ended in June 2007, after 16 years in office.","image":"James Carlisle in 2024.png","birth":1937.5917808219178,"death":null}},"media":{"Flag of Antigua and Barbuda.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Flag_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg/330px-Flag_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg","author":"Original: Sir Reginald Samuel Vector:  David Benbennick","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Antigua and Barbuda.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Coat_of_arms_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg","author":"LadyofHats, based on a bitmap by Ralf Hartemink","license":"Public domain"},"King Charles III (July 2023).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/King_Charles_III_%28July_2023%29.jpg/330px-King_Charles_III_%28July_2023%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Charles_III_(July_2023).jpg","author":"White House","license":"Public domain"},"Gaston Browne Coronation 2023.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Gaston_Browne_Coronation_2023.jpg/330px-Gaston_Browne_Corona